<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<xmile version="1.0" xmlns="http://docs.oasis-open.org/xmile/ns/XMILE/v1.0" xmlns:isee="http://iseesystems.com/XMILE">
	<header>
		<smile version="1.0" namespace="std, isee"/>
		<name>Latest SFD for Preparation Time</name>
		<uuid>20325c0c-c549-4bb2-8124-4383091f5475</uuid>
		<vendor>isee systems, inc.</vendor>
		<product version="2.1.3" isee:build_number="2455" isee:saved_by_v1="true" lang="en">Stella Architect</product>
	</header>
	<sim_specs isee:sim_duration="1.5" isee:simulation_delay="0.107143" isee:restore_on_start="false" method="Euler" time_units="Weeks" isee:instantaneous_flows="false" isee:loop_scores="true" isee:loop_exhaustive_allowed="1000">
		<start>0</start>
		<stop>14</stop>
		<dt reciprocal="true">4</dt>
	</sim_specs>
	<isee:prefs show_module_prefix="true" live_update_on_drag="true" show_restore_buttons="false" layer="model" interface_scale_ui="true" interface_max_page_width="10000" interface_max_page_height="10000" interface_min_page_width="0" interface_min_page_height="0" rerun_on_structure_change="false" saved_runs="5" keep="false" rifp="true"/>
	<isee:multiplayer_settings include_chat="true" allow_observers="false" advance_time_increment="1" max_advance_time_in_ms="0" observer_start_page="home_page" enabled="false"/>
	<isee:time_formats default_format="Builtin">
		<isee:time_format name="Builtin" type="adaptive"/>
	</isee:time_formats>
	<default_format/>
	<model_units>
		<unit name="Dimensionless">
			<eqn>1</eqn>
			<alias>dmnl</alias>
			<alias>unitless</alias>
			<alias>fraction</alias>
		</unit>
		<unit name="Meters">
			<eqn/>
			<alias>m</alias>
			<alias>meter</alias>
		</unit>
		<unit name="Weeks">
			<eqn/>
			<alias>wk</alias>
			<alias>week</alias>
		</unit>
		<unit name="Minutes">
			<eqn/>
			<alias>min</alias>
			<alias>minute</alias>
		</unit>
	</model_units>
	<model>
		<variables>
			<stock name="Convenience Per\nIndividual Group">
				<doc>Items the orchestras have parked in the shared inventory area for their own convenience, which must be moved before a rehearsal. Starts at 27 items. The more items are parked there, the faster each orchestra&apos;s convenience grows (links to both Growth of Convenience flows).</doc>
				<eqn>27</eqn>
				<inflow>Availability_of_Shared_Inventory_Area</inflow>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>items</units>
			</stock>
			<flow name="Availability of\nShared Inventory\nArea">
				<doc>Items parked in the shared area for convenience each week. Orchestras only park more items while there is free space, so the inflow = 0.5 items per week for every m2 of free space (capacity - total occupancy). The fuller the area, the fewer new items are parked (the - link of B1/B2); it stops when the area is full. Starts at 0.5 x (20 - 4) = 8 items per week.</doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, 0.5 * (Capacity_of_Shared_Inventory_Area - Total_Occupancy_of_Shared_Inventory_Area))</eqn>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>items/Weeks</units>
			</flow>
			<aux name="Capacity of Shared Inventory Area">
				<doc>Floor area of the shared inventory area (m2).</doc>
				<eqn>20</eqn>
				<units>m*m</units>
			</aux>
			<stock name="Convenience for Symphony Orchestra">
				<doc>How convenient the Symphony Orchestra finds it to keep its items in the shared inventory area (0 = not at all, 1 = fully). Starts at 0.2.</doc>
				<eqn>0.2</eqn>
				<inflow>Growth_of_Convenience_for_Symphony_Orchestra</inflow>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>Items</units>
			</stock>
			<flow name="Growth of Convenience for Symphony Orchestra">
				<doc>Logistic growth of the Symphony Orchestra&apos;s convenience. R2: the more space it already occupies, the more of a habit parking there becomes (first bracket); growth slows as it nears its 12 m2 maximum (second bracket). B2: it also grows faster when more items are already parked in the shared area (Convenience Per Individual Occupancy / 27, where 27 = the normal number of parked items, so the factor starts at 1); as the area fills, parking slows and so does this growth. 0.2 per week = growth rate.</doc>
				<eqn>0.2 * (Symphony_Orchestra&apos;s_Occupancy_for_Shared_Inventory_Area / 12) * (1 - Symphony_Orchestra&apos;s_Occupancy_for_Shared_Inventory_Area / 12) * Convenience_Per_Individual_Group / 27</eqn>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>items/Weeks</units>
			</flow>
			<aux name="Symphony Orchestra's\nOccupancy\nfor Shared Inventory Area">
				<doc>Floor area of the shared inventory area used by the Symphony Orchestra. 12 = area (m2) its items would take at full convenience (1.0).</doc>
				<eqn>12*Convenience_for_Symphony_Orchestra</eqn>
				<units>Itmes / Week</units>
			</aux>
			<stock name="Convenience for\nChinese Orchestra">
				<doc>How convenient the Chinese Orchestra finds it to keep its items in the shared inventory area (0 = not at all, 1 = fully). Starts at 0.2.</doc>
				<eqn>0.2</eqn>
				<inflow>Growth_of_Convenience_for_Chinese_Orchestra</inflow>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>Items</units>
			</stock>
			<flow name="Growth of Convenience\nfor Chinese Orchestra">
				<doc>Same logic as the Symphony Orchestra (R1 own habit, B1 through the shared area), with a smaller maximum (8 m2) and a slower growth rate (0.15 per week).</doc>
				<eqn>0.15 * (Chinese_Orchestra&apos;s_Occupancy_for_Shared_Inventory_Area / 8) * (1 - Chinese_Orchestra&apos;s_Occupancy_for_Shared_Inventory_Area / 8) * Convenience_Per_Individual_Group / 27</eqn>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>items/Weeks</units>
			</flow>
			<aux name="Chinese Orchestra's\nOccupancy\nfor Shared Inventory Area">
				<doc>Floor area of the shared inventory area used by the Chinese Orchestra. 8 = area (m2) its items would take at full convenience (1.0).</doc>
				<eqn>8*Convenience_for_Chinese_Orchestra</eqn>
				<units>Items / Week</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Total Occupancy of Shared Inventory Area">
				<doc>Floor area of the shared inventory area occupied by both orchestras. Starts at 4 m2 and approaches 20 m2 (= Shared Area Capacity).</doc>
				<eqn>Chinese_Orchestra&apos;s_Occupancy_for_Shared_Inventory_Area+Symphony_Orchestra&apos;s_Occupancy_for_Shared_Inventory_Area</eqn>
				<units>m*m</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Time to Clear the\nInventory Area">
				<doc>Minutes needed to clear the inventory area = items to move / (items per minute per helper x helpers).</doc>
				<eqn>Convenience_Per_Individual_Group/(Speed_to_Clean_up_the_Items_Inventory_Area*Number_of_Student_Helping)</eqn>
				<units>Minutes</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Speed to Clean up\nthe Items Inventory Area">
				<doc>Items one helper can move out of the inventory area per minute (0.4, i.e. 2.5 min per item).</doc>
				<eqn>0.4</eqn>
				<units>items/min/students</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Total Preparation Time">
				<doc>Total preparation time = time to clear the inventory area + time to clear the practice room. About 15 min in week 0, rising in a goal-seeking curve (fast at first, then levelling off) to about 45 min in week 14.</doc>
				<eqn>Time_to_Clear_the_Inventory_Area + Time_to_Clean_up_Unattended_Items</eqn>
				<units>Minutes</units>
			</aux>
			<stock name="Items Left in the Room">
				<doc>Unattended items (chairs, stands, cases) left lying in the practice room. Starts at 12.</doc>
				<eqn>12</eqn>
				<inflow>Weekly_Growth_of_Unattended_Items</inflow>
				<outflow>Weekly_Clear_of_Unattended_Items</outflow>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>items</units>
			</stock>
			<flow name="Weekly Growth of\nUnattended Items">
				<doc>Items left behind each week (40 x 0.13 = 5.2) minus the items the helpers put back during a short tidy-up after rehearsal (2 min per week x 0.5 items per min x helpers). With 5 helpers the net is 0.2 items per week; it rises to about 0.55 as helpers drop out. MAX(0, ...) because the flow cannot be negative.</doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0,Number_of_Items_Used-Room_Usage_Shortfall*Number_of_Student_Helping*Speed_to_Clean_up_items_in_Practice_Room)</eqn>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>items/Weeks</units>
			</flow>
			<aux name="Desired Room Space">
				<doc>Free floor area needed to set up the ensemble for a rehearsal (m2).</doc>
				<eqn>72</eqn>
				<units>m*m</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Room Space Capacity">
				<doc>Floor area of the practice room (m2).</doc>
				<eqn>80</eqn>
				<units>m*m</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Current Room Space Available">
				<doc>Free floor area = room area minus the area blocked by unattended items. 1 = m2 blocked by one item. Cannot go below 0.</doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, Room_Space_Capacity - 1 * Items_Left_in_the_Room)</eqn>
				<units>m*m</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Number of Items to be Cleaned up">
				<doc>Items that must be moved to get back to the desired free space = missing space / 1 m2 per item. With 80 m2 and 72 m2 desired, 8 items can stay along the walls; every item beyond that must be moved.</doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, Desired_Room_Space - Current_Room_Space_Available) / 1</eqn>
				<units>items</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Speed to Clean up\nitems in Practice Room">
				<doc>Items one helper can clear in the practice room per minute (0.5, i.e. 2 min per item).</doc>
				<eqn>0.5</eqn>
				<units>items/min/students</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Time to Clean up\nUnattended Items">
				<doc>Minutes needed to clear the practice room = items to move / (items per minute per helper x helpers).</doc>
				<eqn>Number_of_Items_to_be_Cleaned_up / (Speed_to_Clean_up_items_in_Practice_Room * Number_of_Student_Helping)</eqn>
				<units>Minutes</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Room Usage Shortfall">
				<doc>Fraction of the items used that are not put back after the room is used (13%).</doc>
				<eqn>5</eqn>
				<units>min / week</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Number of Items Used">
				<doc>Items taken out and used in the practice room each week.</doc>
				<eqn>40</eqn>
				<units>items/Weeks</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Willingness To Help">
				<doc>Share of the original helpers who are still willing to help. It is 1 (everyone) when preparation takes the normal 15 min, and it falls by 0.0025 for every extra minute (e.g. 0.925 at 45 min), because a longer chore puts students off. MAX(0, ...) keeps it from going below 0.</doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, 1 - 0.0025 * (Total_Preparation_Time - 15))</eqn>
				<units>Dimensionless</units>
			</aux>
			<stock name="Number of\nStudent Helping">
				<doc>Students who help with the preparation each week. Starts at 5. It can only fall (one outflow): helpers drop out when the preparation becomes a longer chore.</doc>
				<eqn>8</eqn>
				<outflow>Decrease_Rate_of_Student_Helping</outflow>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>students</units>
			</stock>
			<flow name="Decrease Rate of Student Helping">
				<doc>Helpers who are no longer willing drop out gradually. Gap = current helpers - willing helpers, where willing helpers = starting helpers (INIT = 5) x Willingness To Help. 2 = weeks it takes an unwilling helper to stop turning up. MAX(0, ...) because helpers only leave through this flow.</doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, Number_of_Student_Helping - INIT(Number_of_Student_Helping) * Willingness_To_Help) / 2</eqn>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>students/Weeks</units>
			</flow>
			<flow name="Weekly Clear\nof\nUnattended Items">
				<eqn>Time_to_Clean_up_Unattended_Items*Speed_to_Clean_up_items_in_Practice_Room</eqn>
				<non_negative/>
				<units>items/Weeks</units>
			</flow>
		</variables>
